# Unguarded admin route (CWE-862). KEUR-NEST-001 only matches delete/remove/drop
# substrings in the route path; an /admin* handler with no @UseGuards and no
# global guard is reachable by anyone who knows the path. mestjs gap #7
# (docs/KEUR-COVERAGE-GAPS.md).
id: KEUR-NEST-015
title: Admin route handler with no guard (NestJS)
category: security
severity: warning
engine: multiline
window: 4
skip_comments: true
target:
  extensions: .ts
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ node_modules/ dist/ build/ _spec/
patterns:
  # @Get/@Post/... on a path containing 'admin', with NO @UseGuards on the
  # preceding/same lines in the window.
  - regex: (?s)@(?:Get|Post|Put|Delete|Patch)\s*\(\s*[`''"][^`''"]*admin[^`''"]*[`''"]\s*\)\s*.{0,80}?\b\w+\s*\(
    exclude: @UseGuards
    message: "An @-route whose path contains 'admin' has no @UseGuards — direct-request to a privileged handler (CWE-862): anyone who knows the path reaches it. Add @UseGuards(AuthGuard/RolesGuard) or a global guard, and require an admin role."
confidence: 0.55
fix: "Protect admin handlers with @UseGuards(...) + a role check, or register a global guard that default-denies admin paths."
